# Tests.AnchorsSimd — D335 (V1a): the packed-integer arithmetic pins, in a module of their own

Arm (A) of the 2026-10-10 kernel-cost fork. Inside `Tests.Anchors` these 396 `decide` pins moved that module's kernel
unfoldings from 2,878,319 to 6,377,905 against a relative allowance of 670,648 (`ku_delta.py --arm a-prime`, D335's
Result). In a module of their own they are a NEW unit, judged once against an absolute registration measured on its
own machine (`scripts/kernel_ceilings.txt`, `scripts/ku_delta_budget.txt`), and `Tests.Anchors` keeps its budget —
D311's rule (one test module per witness family), applied to a family that is all one probe.

The block between the markers is GENERATED by `hwprobe/mk_simda_anchors.py` (`--check` gates it byte for byte).

LANE. Personal lane, public sources only.
-/
import X86

namespace X86.Tests.Simd
open X86

/-! ## D335 (V1a) — eleven SSE-legacy packed-integer arithmetic mnemonics against a processor's reading

⚠️ NONE OF THESE HAS A DIFFERENTIAL PARTNER: ACL2 x86isa refuses PMADDWD, PMADDUBSW, PMULLW, PMULHRSW, PMULUDQ,
PADDSW, PSUBUSW, PSUBUSB, PMAXSW, PSADBW and PACKSSDW at every pre-state.  So the rows below — run by
`hwprobe/simda_probe.c` on a hosted runner's processor, derived from the SDM's rules by `hwprobe/mk_simda_rows.py` —
are the only check of this model's numbers for them, and every row is pinned.

The pre-state is the probe's (`hwprobe/simda_ops.S`): %xmm0 = DEST (all 128 bits), %xmm1 = SRC, the m128 at RBX holds
the same SRC (16-byte aligned, as a legacy-SSE m128 must be), and the six arithmetic flags are the row's `f`.  A row
agrees when the step did not refuse, %xmm0 is the row's 128 bits, %xmm1 and the m128 are unchanged, the six flags are
exactly `f` — "Flags Affected: None" — and RIP moved by the instruction's length. -/

/-- The six arithmetic flags of an RFLAGS image (CF PF AF ZF SF OF at bits 0 2 4 6 7 11); DF stays clear —
`Tests.Anchors`' `w1bFlags`, restated because that one is private to its module. -/
private def v1aFlags (f : BitVec 64) : Flags :=
  ⟨f.getLsbD 0, f.getLsbD 2, f.getLsbD 4, f.getLsbD 6, f.getLsbD 7, f.getLsbD 11, false⟩

/-- The RFLAGS image of the flags this model keeps, at `flagFields`' positions (`Tests.Anchors`' `b0Rflags`). -/
private def v1aRflags (f : Flags) : BitVec 64 :=
  flagFields.foldl (fun acc r => acc ||| (if r.get f then (1 : BitVec 64) <<< r.bit else 0)) 0

/-- `simda_ops.S`'s pre-state, at RIP 0x400000 with the m128 source at 0x2000 (16-byte aligned). -/
private def v1aPre (a b : BitVec 128) (f : BitVec 64) : Cpu :=
  ((({ regs := ({} : Regs).set .rbx 0x2000, flags := v1aFlags f, mem := {}, rip := 0x400000,
       oracle := Oracle.zero } : Cpu).setXmm .x0 a).setXmm .x1 b).writeMem128 0x2000 b

private def v1aAgrees (t : Cpu) (n : Nat) (b : BitVec 128) (f : BitVec 64) (w : BitVec 128) : Bool :=
  t.ms.isNone && t.getXmm .x0 == w && t.getXmm .x1 == b && t.readMem128 0x2000 == b
    && (v1aRflags t.flags &&& 0x8d5) == (f &&& 0x8d5) && t.rip == 0x400000 + BitVec.ofNat 64 n

